WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.400
Suppliers, customers, landlords and employers.

2
00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:08.910
This is the video for Module 3 of Negotiation Skills for Business and Life.

3
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:22.280
Every naira you save when buying, and every naira you protect when selling, goes straight to your profit. These are long-term relationships, so aim for deals the other side is happy to repeat.

4
00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:32.020
Landlords and employers have more formal power than you. Good preparation, respect and objective evidence help balance that power.

5
00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:44.280
A low unit price can hide costs. Always compare suppliers on landed cost. That is the price per unit plus delivery, packaging and losses from damaged goods.

6
00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:54.750
Supplier A charges 1900 a yard, all upfront, plus 8000 delivery. Landed cost, 388000 naira.

7
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:09.560
Supplier B charges 1950, with free delivery, and half now, half after delivery. Landed cost, 390000. Only 2000 more, and paying half later helps her cash flow.

8
00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:20.780
So Rukayat asks B. If I order 300 yards for the next two terms, can you do a better price on the same terms? B offers 1900.

9
00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:28.570
Now she gets A's price with B's better terms, paying 285000 now and the rest after delivery.

10
00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:35.370
Customers often ask, what is the last price? That is normal and friendly. Plan for it.

11
00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:46.000
If a dress costs you 9000 to make and you sell at 15000, a 3000 discount cuts your profit in half, from 6000 to 3000.

12
00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:53.540
So offer value instead. Free delivery in your area, a small extra item, or faster finishing.

13
00:01:54.790 --> 00:02:00.340
Use quantity breaks, for example 15000 each, or 42000 for three.

14
00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:09.970
For custom work, many tailors, caterers and bakers ask a deposit of 50% to 70% before buying materials.

15
00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:19.080
With landlords, gather evidence first. Ask three other tenants in the area what they pay, and note leaks or broken things.

16
00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:26.960
More than the amount can be discussed. Ask to pay in two instalments, and agree who fixes what before you pay.

17
00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:32.840
Ask for receipts for every fee, and whether the caution deposit is refundable.

18
00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:41.530
Inspect the property in person, and speak to the landlord directly. Pay into an account in the landlord's or agency's name.

19
00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:54.130
Fake agents collect money for places they do not own. If a demand seems unusual, ask a lawyer, a tenants' association or a trusted community leader before you pay.

20
00:02:55.380 --> 00:03:10.850
Blessing has taken over stock records and set up the shop's WhatsApp ordering. Friends in similar roles earn roughly 110000 to 130000. Her walk-away is 105000, plus a clear review date.

21
00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:19.970
She earns 90000 a month. She books a quiet time and opens. I enjoy working here and I want to grow with the business.

22
00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:28.690
She shows evidence, fewer stock losses and a list of WhatsApp orders, and asks for 125000.

23
00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:37.580
The owner says 100000 is the most he can do now. She asks, what would make 120000 possible?

24
00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:48.380
They agree 110000 now, and a review to 120000 in three months tied to WhatsApp sales. She asks for it in writing.

25
00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:55.300
If pay cannot move, try other tradeables: transport allowance, title, training, or flexible hours.

26
00:03:56.550 --> 00:04:05.690
Relationships and respect matter as much as numbers. Uche greets the trader by name first. Mama Chidi, good morning, how is the family?

27
00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:15.620
The trader asks 95000 for beans. Uche has checked two other stalls. Mama, you know I buy from you every week. Help me.

28
00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:28.540
She adds the tomatoes to her order to strengthen her offer. Beans settle at 88000, saving her 7000, and the trader adds a few extra tomatoes as jara.

29
00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:33.310
You may keep your walk-away point private. That is acceptable.

30
00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:46.550
But never state things you know are false. Trust, once lost, costs far more than one deal. In a community where people talk, your reputation for fair dealing is one of your strongest assets.

31
00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:57.010
To remember. Compare suppliers on landed cost. Give value before you cut price. Never pay rent before you inspect and verify the owner.

32
00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:05.020
Bring evidence to a pay talk. And keep your limit private, but never state false facts. Confirm every agreement in writing.

33
00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:17.710
Now your turn. Work out the landed cost from two suppliers, prepare for a rent or pay talk with three pieces of evidence, and write your own three rules for honest negotiation.

34
00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:20.000
Continue with the lessons below.
